sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant PS as pytest / asyncio
    participant PHY as BabbleSim PHY
    participant CH as BsimClock (in pytest)<br/>d=4
    participant VC0 as Virtual Controller 0<br/>d=0
    participant VC1 as Virtual Controller 1<br/>d=1
    participant CEN as Central App<br/>d=2
    participant PER as Peripheral App<br/>d=3

    Note over PS,PER: Phase 1 — Create the complete simulation world

    rect rgb(240, 246, 255)
        PS->>PHY: spawn bs_2G4_phy_v1<br/>-D=5 -defmodem=BLE_simple
        PHY-->>PS: PHY ready

        PS->>VC0: spawn bt_virt_controller<br/>-d=0 -hci-socket=hci0.sock
        PS->>VC1: spawn bt_virt_controller<br/>-d=1 -hci-socket=hci1.sock

        PS->>PS: wait for HCI sockets
        Note over VC0,VC1: hci0.sock / hci1.sock ready

        PS->>CEN: spawn Central<br/>d=2 --bt-dev=hci0.sock
        PS->>PER: spawn Peripheral<br/>d=3 --bt-dev=hci1.sock

        PS->>CH: connect through FIFOs<br/>register pytest as d=4

        PS->>PS: wait for 5 BabbleSim device locks
        Note over PHY,PER: d=0,1,2,3,4 register to the same PHY

        PHY-->>PS: all devices registered
    end

    Note over PS,PER: Simulation topology is now fully constructed

    rect rgb(245, 238, 255)
        Note over CEN,VC0: CENTRAL → hci0.sock → VC0 → PHY
        Note over PER,VC1: PERIPHERAL → hci1.sock → VC1 → PHY
        Note over PHY: Shared 2.4 GHz RF medium<br/>attenuation = 45 dB
    end

    Note over PS,PER: Phase 2 — Deterministic discrete-time execution

    rect rgb(235, 248, 240)
        PS->>PS: process callbacks and ready I/O at t0
        PS->>CH: advance_to_us(t1)<br/>only when selector would block
        CH->>PHY: WAIT through FIFO
        PHY->>VC0: advance
        PHY->>VC1: advance
        PHY->>CEN: advance
        PHY->>PER: advance

        Note over PHY,PER: All simulated devices execute within this 10 ms window

        CH-->>PS: now_us

        Note over PS,PER: Virtual Time = t1
        PS->>PS: dispatch I/O / timers / assertions
        Note over PS,PER: pytest processing does NOT advance simulation time
    end

    rect rgb(235, 248, 240)
        PS->>CH: advance_to_us(t2)<br/>only when selector would block again
        CH->>PHY: WAIT(end = t2)
        PHY->>VC0: advance
        PHY->>VC1: advance
        PHY->>CEN: advance
        PHY->>PER: advance

        CH-->>PS: now_us

        Note over PS,PER: Virtual Time = t2
        PS->>PS: process events generated by this step
    end

    Note over PS,PER: ready work → WAIT → barrier → asyncio dispatch → ready work → ...

    rect rgb(255, 248, 235)
        Note over PER,CEN: BLE behavior emerges while discrete time is repeatedly advanced

        PER->>VC1: HCI commands via hci1.sock
        VC1->>PHY: Advertising PDU

        PHY-->>VC0: Simulated RF
        VC0-->>CEN: Advertising Report via hci0.sock

        CEN->>VC0: HCI commands
        VC0->>PHY: Connection traffic
        PHY-->>VC1: Simulated RF
        VC1-->>PER: Connection event

        CEN-->>PS: Connected

        PER->>VC1: GATT Notification
        VC1->>PHY: BLE Data PDU
        PHY-->>VC0: Simulated RF
        VC0-->>CEN: HCI Notification

        CEN-->>PS: [NOTIFICATION]
    end
